rhood, but the timing does not cooperate. 1006's five events fall in bursts near 20431-21630, 40832-41431 and 46832-47431; 1860's five events fall near 19831-20430, 26432-27031, 32432-33631 and 43232-43831. 1860's first inbound event precedes all 1006 activity; the next one is >4800 units after 1006's first burst; and the 43232-43831 event is >1800 units after 1006's second burst, exceeding the 1200-unit reach of the short 3-hop route under a 600-unit relay limit. 1006's final burst postdates every 1860 event. Hence the observed volume and static connectivity are confounders, not evidence of a genuine time-respecting cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structural check (steps 01\u201302):** In the window there are 7,200 events over 1,941 nodes with a nearly non-repeating edge set (repeat_ratio 0.016). A static path does exist: 1006\u219245, and 45\u2192153 / 45\u2192182, with 153\u21921860 and 182\u21921860 all present in the 2-hop subgraph. So an ignore-time connection exists \u2014 this is precisely the confounder to control for.\n\n**Endpoint contact sets (steps 03\u201304):** 1006 has only 4 outgoing partners (45, 230, 925, 1680); 1860 has only 4 incoming partners (153, 182, 958, 1390). Any cascade must exit through the former and enter through the latter.\n\n**Temporal localisation (steps 05\u201308):** Both endpoints are very sparse (\u22485 events each).\n- 1006's activity sits in three tight bursts: ~[20431, 21630], ~[40832, 41431], ~[46832, 47431].\n- 1860's events sit at ~[19831, 20430], ~[26432, 27031], ~[32432, 33631], ~[43232, 43831].\n\nConsequences under the 600-unit relay constraint:\n- 1860's **earliest** inbound event (~19831\u201320430) *precedes* all of 1006's activity \u2192 cannot be downstream.\n- After 1006's first burst (\u226421630), the next 1860 inbound event is \u226526432 \u2014 a dead interval of \u22654,800 units, requiring \u22659 perfectly chained hops.\n- After 1006's second burst (\u226441431), the next 1860 inbound event is \u226543232 \u2014 a gap of \u22651,801 units, so the short 1006\u219245\u2192{153,182}\u21921860 route (max reach 1,800 units) is *excluded*.\n- 1006's last burst (\u226546832) is after every 1860 event.\n\nSo no 2- or 3-hop time-respecting relay is possible, and the only remaining options demand long chains across intervals where neither endpoint is active \u2014 implausible in a graph this sparse and non-repetitive.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_30df0d06\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 45, 153, 182, 230, 925, 1680, 958, 1390],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.63,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A time-ignoring path 1006->45->{153,182}->1860 exists (step_02), and both nodes touch a hub-rich neighbourhood, but the timing does not cooperate. 1006's five events fall in bursts near 20431-21630, 40832-41431 and 46832-47431; 1860's five events fall near 19831-20430, 26432-27031, 32432-33631 and 43232-43831. 1860's first inbound event precedes all 1006 activity; the next one is >4800 units after 1006's first burst; and the 43232-43831 event is >1800 units after 1006's second burst, exceeding the 1200-unit reach of the short 3-hop route under a 600-unit relay limit. 1006's final burst postdates every 1860 event. Hence the observed volume and static connectivity are confounders, not evidence of a genuine time-respecting cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 26278, "total_output_tokens": 7075, "